# Fetched tape. Large, reproducible, and it changes every hour -- committing it
# would make the diff useless and the repo heavy. Re-fetch with any data
# command, or `discover-markets` + `backtest`.
data/raw/*.json

# Runtime state is per-machine and per-run: nonces, health, budgets, soak.
# A nonce store in particular must NEVER be shared between machines.
state/*.json
state/*.tmp

# The kill switch is an operational act, never a committed file. The .example
# is tracked; the switch itself is not.
runtime/KILL_SWITCH

# Generated reports. All of them: the negation that used to sit here kept
# `reports/pnl_baseline.json`, and it was pointing at the wrong copy --
# MEASURED byte-identical to `docs/pnl_baseline.json`, which is tracked and is
# the path the changelog entry actually cites. Two copies of one piece of
# evidence is how the two drift, and the `reports/` one is rewritten by any
# run of `dashboard_patch`. The canonical baseline lives in `docs/`.
# `.gitkeep` is NOT matched, so the directory stays tracked.
reports/*.json
reports/*.log

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
